      "body": "Co-authored-by: OpenAI Codex\n\n\n\n## Overview\nDocument the aggregation semantics of NIXL KV connector metrics across TP ranks.\nRelated to #41230.\n\n\n## Claims\n- Clarify that NIXL metrics are computed from pooled rank-level transfer observations.\n- Explain that average payload size, means, and P90s use the combined observation pool.\n- Document throughput as total transfer volume divided by summed transfer durations.\n- Describe the logging pipeline and clarify that `observe()` receives statistics already aggregated across workers.\n\n\n## Validation\nRan pre-commit checks on both modified files:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files \\\n  vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/nixl/stats.py \\\n  vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/metrics.py\n```\nResult: **Passed**.\n\nChecked the committed patch for whitespace errors:\n\n```bash\ngit show --check HEAD\n```\nResult: **Passed**.\n\n\n## Details\nThe changes are limited to docstrings and inline comments.\n\nAI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used for documentation wording and validation.\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
